{#- TWO TABS, ONE HEADER. The console's navigation is full, and these are two
   halves of the same job: things published to the public site, as opposed to
   Content next door, which is the site's WORDS one language at a time. The
   Ministry page already holds four tools under one entry this way, and
   staff.js wires `.tabs` / `.tab-panel` generically, hash included.

   A third collection later is a third tab, not a ninth header. -#}

<div class="tabs" role="tablist">
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="resources"
          aria-selected="true" data-i18n="lib.resources">Resources</button>
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="gatherings"
          aria-selected="false" data-i18n="lib.gatherings">Gatherings</button>
</div>

{#- LANGUAGES ARE OPTIONAL PER ITEM, and the note says so where somebody is
   about to hit it. The site's chrome carries every language always because it
   is written once at a desk; these are written in the field, in a hurry, in
   whichever language the person has. A save is never refused for a missing
   translation, and the public page shows the item with a marker rather than
   hiding it. -#}
<p class="note">
  <b>Publish in whatever language you have.</b> A translation can follow later
  and nothing here waits for it — an item with only Croatian appears to English
  readers with a small note, rather than disappearing.
</p>

<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="resources" role="tabpanel">
  <div class="ms-bar">
    <button type="button" class="solid-btn" data-lib-add="resources"
            data-i18n="lib.addResource">+ Add resource</button>
  </div>
  <div class="adm-people" data-lib-list="resources">
    <p class="empty" data-i18n="common.loading">Loading&hellip;</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="gatherings" role="tabpanel" hidden>
  <div class="ms-bar">
    <button type="button" class="solid-btn" data-lib-add="gatherings"
            data-i18n="lib.addGathering">+ Add gathering</button>
  </div>
  <div class="adm-people" data-lib-list="gatherings">
    <p class="empty" data-i18n="common.loading">Loading&hellip;</p>
  </div>
</section>

{#- The languages this build publishes, handed to the script rather than
   fetched: it is the same list Eleventy paginated the public pages over, so
   the editor cannot offer a language the site does not render. -#}
<script id="libLangs" type="application/json">{{ activeLangs | dump | safe }}</script>
